    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "It follows directly from the definition that sums of noncentral $ \\chi^{2} $ variables also follows a noncentral $ \\chi^{2} $ distribution, so that if $ u \\sim \\chi_{n,\\lambda_{1}}^{2} $ and $ v \\sim \\chi_{m,\\lambda_{2}}^{2} $, then",
      "source_page": 891,
      "printed_page": 871,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "p891:b4"
      ],
      "bbox": [
